(Cohen's d is the mean difference divided by the pooled standard deviation \(below 0.2 negligible, 0.2-0.5 small, 0.5-0.8 medium, above 0.8) Tj
T* (large\). Total variation is half the summed absolute difference between the two histograms. Wasserstein-1 is the area between the two) Tj
T* (cumulative distributions, in index units. No p-value is given for window differences because neighbouring pixels are spatially) Tj
T* (autocorrelated, which makes naive tests overconfident.) Tj
